# Development happens on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise
# commit CRLF and hand it back on checkout. Two separate hazards follow, so
# there are two halves to this file.

# --- 1. Files that are executed or parsed rather than just read --------------
# A stray CR breaks a shell heredoc terminator and is passed through into
# container builds. `.env` is the sharpest case: docker-compose.yml reads it with
# env_file, so a trailing CR ends up inside the value -- SATVA_DEBUG=true\r and
# SATVA_ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL_MIN=60\r both fail pydantic-settings coercion and the
# API container dies on startup. The documented first step is
# `cp .env.example .env`, so the example has to be pinned too.
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.conf  text eol=lf
*.ini   text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# --- 2. Files that must never be touched at all ------------------------------
# Without an explicit attribute Git guesses text vs binary from a NUL byte in
# the first 8000 bytes only. A model whose header happens to be NUL-free would
# have every 0x0D 0x0A pair rewritten, silently corrupting the weights the
# mobile colorimetry engine loads -- and it would surface as wrong inference
# output, not as a load error.
*.tflite  binary
*.onnx    binary
*.pb      binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.webp    binary
*.ico     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
# TensorFlow SavedModel weights: extensionless, so the globs above miss them.
# Scoped to variables/ on purpose -- ml/artifacts also holds JSON reports that
# should stay diffable.
ml/artifacts/saved_model/variables/**  binary
